ors  there are several types of sensuality  measures and so just to highlight for  you can think about things like degree  centrality right you know the more  connections a note has the more  important it has which is in contrast  between the centrality between the  centrality as well if given all the  shortest paths from all nodes to all  other nodes which nodes sit in the  middle of the most paths and that's a  very different idea than I ghen vector  centrality or pagerank sexuality or cat  centrality which think well you know  it's not just about you it's about you  being connected to other important nodes  you know what I you know hopefully you  can observe here is that the color is is  a scale color continuous color that the  darker it is the more important that  note is and the different centrality  measures give you different metrics and  the questions that we want to start to  ask is well how important are our time  structures also how important are our  key phrases related to these time  structures so just to take a little cut  here and I really couldn't figure out a  good way to  visualize this but to that graph I've  applied both between the centrality and  cat centrality and then rank them and so  you can see we have both weeks and  phrases right because they're both  vertices in the graph so week 40 is more  between than week 2 which is more  between than week 45 which could sort of  show that these weeks have more terms  that are sort of more global whereas we  have a different ordering of weeks when  you look at the the cat centrality then  when you start to look at the terms  themselves in there between this you can  start to see things like turnout  Democratic undocumented immigrants big  issue in week 45 verses in week 1 rows  local pastry dessert lemon but you start  to see like the feels like there's  actually sort of something connecting  things here in the cast centrality you  can see citizen natholi finance big  efficiency sweet party delegate